  </ul>
  <p>To sell an ebook online with Gumroad, create a product, upload your ebook as a PDF or EPUB file, set a price, and publish it. Gumroad gives your ebook a product page, takes the payment, and sends each buyer a receipt with a link to the ebook. You don't need your own website.</p>
  <p>Your buyers can download the ebook, read it in their browser, read it in the Gumroad app, or send it to their Kindle.</p>

  <h3 id="Choose-your-ebook-file-formats-Kd3mP">Choose your ebook file formats</h3>
  <p>You can upload your ebook in one format or in several. Each format works differently for your buyers:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>PDF.</strong> A PDF keeps your page layout, and most devices can open one. Buyers can download it, read it in their browser, or send it to a Kindle. PDF is the only format Gumroad can stamp with the buyer's email address.</li>
    <li><strong>EPUB.</strong> EPUB text reflows to fit the screen, so it is easier to read on phones and e-readers. Buyers can download it, read it in their browser, or send it to a Kindle.</li>
    <li><strong>MOBI.</strong> Buyers can download a MOBI file. Gumroad doesn't show the Read or Send to Kindle buttons for it.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>If you can make only one format, upload a PDF. If you can make two, add an EPUB. When a product has a PDF and no EPUB, the Content tab reminds you to add one.</p>
  <p>Two size limits affect how buyers can read your ebook:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Send to Kindle works for PDF and EPUB files under 15.5 MB.</li>
    <li>The browser reader opens EPUB files up to 32 MB. Buyers can still download a larger EPUB.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="Create-your-ebook-product-Wq7nT">Create your ebook product</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>Go to your <a href="https://gumroad.com/products">Products page</a>, and click <strong>New product</strong>.</li>
    <li>Enter the title of your ebook in <strong>Name</strong>.</li>
    <li>Under <strong>Products</strong>, select <strong>E-book</strong>.</li>
    <li>Enter a <strong>Price</strong>. You can change it later.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Next: Customize</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>The product editor opens on the <strong>Product</strong> tab. Write a description that tells readers what the book covers and who it is for. Then <a href="60-adding-a-cover-image" target="_self">add a cover image</a>.</p>
  <p>Because you chose E-book, Gumroad adds a <strong>Pages</strong> row under <strong>Additional details</strong>, where you can enter your page count. Gumroad also describes your product page to search engines as a book.</p>
  <p>For every other field on this tab, see <a href="149-adding-a-product" target="_self">Adding a product</a>. When you are done, click <strong>Save and continue</strong> to go to the Content tab.</p>

  <h3 id="Upload-your-ebook-files-Hs2vB">Upload your ebook files</h3>
  <ol>
    <li>In the product editor, go to the <strong>Content</strong> tab.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Upload your files</strong>, then click <strong>Computer files</strong>. To upload from Dropbox instead, click <strong>Dropbox files</strong>.</li>
    <li>Choose your ebook files. Each file appears as a row on the page.</li>
    <li>To rename a file, or to add a description or an ISBN, click the arrow on the file's row.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>If the page already has content, the <strong>Upload your files</strong> button is gone. Use <strong>Upload files</strong> in the editor toolbar instead.</p>
  <p>You can also type on the Content page. For example, add a note that tells buyers which format to choose for their device.</p>

  <h3 id="Set-your-price-Lp9xR">Set your price</h3>
  <p>You set the price when you create the product. To change it, go to the <strong>Product</strong> tab, and enter a new <strong>Amount</strong> under <strong>Pricing</strong>.</p>
  <p>To let readers pay more than your price, turn on <strong>Allow customers to pay what they want</strong>. Your Amount becomes the minimum. You can also enter a <strong>Suggested amount</strong>.</p>
  <p>To give your ebook away, set the Amount to 0. Gumroad then turns on pay what you want, so readers can pay nothing or choose to pay. See <a href="133-pay-what-you-want-pricing" target="_self">"Pay what you want" pricing</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="Protect-your-PDF-with-PDF-stamping-Zc4gM">Protect your PDF with PDF stamping</h3>
  <p>PDF stamping adds "Sold to" and the buyer's email address to the bottom right corner of the first page of their copy. A buyer is less likely to share a file that has their email address on it.</p>
  <p>To turn on PDF stamping:</p>
  <ol>
    <li>In the product editor, go to the <strong>Content</strong> tab.</li>
    <li>Click the arrow on your PDF's row.</li>
    <li>Turn on <strong>Stamp this PDF with buyer information</strong>.</li>
    <li>Click <strong>Save changes</strong>.</li>
  </ol>
  <p>Stamping works only for PDF files. Gumroad can't stamp EPUB or MOBI files. Stamping is not DRM, and Gumroad does not offer DRM. See <a href="130-pdf-stamping" target="_self">PDF stamping</a>.</p>
  <p>You can also stop buyers from downloading a PDF or an EPUB. In the same file settings, turn on <strong>Disable file downloads (buyers read it in the browser instead)</strong>. The file then has no Download button, and buyers open it with the Read button. You can't turn this on for an EPUB over 32 MB.</p>

  <h3 id="Publish-your-ebook-Tn6yJ">Publish your ebook</h3>
  <p>Before you can publish, connect a payout method in your <a href="260-your-payout-settings-page" target="_self">payout settings</a>.</p>
  <p>When your ebook is ready, click <strong>Publish and continue</strong> at the top of the product editor. Gumroad opens the <strong>Share</strong> tab. Click <strong>Copy URL</strong> to copy the link to your product page, and share that link with your readers.</p>
  <p>To see what your buyers get, <a href="62-testing-a-purchase" target="_self">make a test purchase</a>.</p>

  <h3 id="How-buyers-get-and-read-your-ebook-Bf8kD">How buyers get and read your ebook</h3>
  <p>After they pay, your buyers get a receipt by email. The <strong>View content</strong> button in the receipt opens their download page. Buyers who have a Gumroad account also find your ebook in their <a href="247-what-your-customers-see" target="_self">Library</a>.</p>
  <p>On the download page, each file has its own buttons:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Download</strong> saves the file to the buyer's device. They can then open it in any reading app or copy it to an e-reader.</li>
    <li><strong>Read</strong> opens a PDF, or an EPUB up to 32 MB, in the buyer's browser. The reader remembers their place.</li>
    <li><strong>Send to Kindle</strong> emails a PDF or EPUB under 15.5 MB to the buyer's Kindle email address. See <a href="208-how-do-i-send-my-gumroad-purchase-to-my-kindle" target="_self">How do I send my purchases to Kindle?</a></li>
  </ul>
  <p>Buyers can also read PDF and EPUB files in the <a href="177-the-gumroad-dashboard-app" target="_self">Gumroad app</a> for iOS and Android.</p>
  <p>To hide the Read and Send to Kindle buttons for a file, click the arrow on the file's row in the Content tab. Then turn off <strong>Show "Send to Kindle" and "Read" buttons on the download page</strong>.</p>

  <h3 id="Sell-more-copies-of-your-ebook-Rv5wS">Sell more copies of your ebook</h3>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Offer versions.</strong> Sell your ebook at more than one price from the same product page. For example, offer "Ebook" and "Ebook and workbook". On the Product tab, click <strong>Add version</strong> under <strong>Versions</strong>, and enter a <strong>Name</strong> and an <strong>Additional amount</strong>. Then choose each version on the Content tab, and upload its files. See <a href="126-setting-up-versions-on-a-digital-product" target="_self">Setting up versions</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Sell a bundle.</strong> If you have two or more products, such as a series of ebooks, sell them together for one price. Create a new product, and select <strong>Bundle</strong>. See <a href="339-product-bundles" target="_self">Product bundles</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>Create a discount code.</strong> Go to your Checkout page, open the <strong>Discounts</strong> tab, and click <strong>New discount</strong>. Use a code for a launch price or for your newsletter readers. See <a href="128-discount-codes" target="_self">Discount codes</a>.</li>
    <li><strong>List your ebook on Gumroad Discover.</strong> Discover recommends your products to prospective customers. On the Share tab, choose a <strong>Category</strong> and add up to 10 <strong>Tags</strong> that readers would search for. Your account has to meet some requirements first. See <a href="79-gumroad-discover" target="_self">Gumroad Discover</a>.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3 id="Common-questions-about-selling-ebooks-Gj1qN">Common questions about selling ebooks</h3>
  <p><strong>How large can my ebook file be?</strong></p>
  <p>On a paid product, each file can be up to 20 GB. Free products have a lower limit. See <a href="289-file-size-limits-on-gumroad" target="_self">File size limits</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Does Gumroad handle sales tax and VAT on my ebook?</strong></p>
  <p>Yes. Gumroad is the merchant of record for your sales, so Gumroad collects and remits sales tax and VAT. See <a href="121-sales-tax-on-gumroad" target="_self">Sales tax on Gumroad</a>.</p>
  <p>Many EU countries have a lower VAT rate for e-publications. If your ebook qualifies, go to the Product tab, and turn on <strong>Mark product as e-publication for VAT purposes</strong> under <strong>Settings</strong>. See <a href="10-dealing-with-vat" target="_self">EU &amp; UK VAT on Gumroad</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>How much does Gumroad charge when I sell an ebook?</strong></p>
  <p>Gumroad charges 10% + $0.50 for each sale, plus card processing of 2.9% + $0.30. Sales that come through Gumroad Discover have a flat 30% fee instead. There is no monthly fee. See <a href="66-gumroads-fees" target="_self">Gumroad's fees</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>When do I get paid for my ebook sales?</strong></p>
  <p>Your earnings go to your Gumroad balance. Gumroad pays out your balance every week by default, once it reaches $100. Some countries have a higher minimum. See <a href="13-getting-paid" target="_self">Getting paid by Gumroad</a>.</p>
  <p><strong>Do I need an ISBN to sell an ebook on Gumroad?</strong></p>
  <p>No. If your ebook has an ISBN, you can add it. Click the arrow on the file's row in the Content tab, and enter it in the <strong>ISBN</strong> field.</p>
